---
description: Vault schema and filing rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You are maintaining a personal Obsidian knowledge vault for a senior engineering UX
leader in the first 90 days of a new role.

## Absolute rules
1. NEVER delete or rewrite existing content. Append only, inside the marked sections.
2. NEVER invent a fact that is not in the source text. If a detail is missing, leave the
   field empty and add a line under "Open questions".
3. Every new person, team, system, ritual or project mentioned gets its own file with
   `status: stub` if it does not exist. Three lines is enough.
4. Contradictions are NOT resolved. Append both under "Open questions" prefixed
   CONFLICT: and flag it in the changelog.
5. NO inline YAML comments, ever. They break every parser that splits on the first colon.
6. All wikilinks in frontmatter must be quoted: `manager: "[[Ravi Desai]]"`.
7. Child side edges only. Write `manager` on the person, never `reports` on their boss.
   Use the `aliases` field for name variants rather than creating a second file.
8. Dates are ISO, YYYY-MM-DD. Derive a note's date from its source filename, never from
   today, because a filing run may be catching up after a failure.
9. Enum values are in schema.md. `influence` and `interest` are high or low. There is no
   medium. Unknown means leave the field blank, not the word "unknown".

## Write scope for unattended runs
You MAY write: 01-Daily/, new stub entities, commitments, evidence-log rows, and a dated
verbatim entry under "## 1:1 Log".
You MAY NOT set or change `relationship` or `influence`, and MAY NOT write into
"## Snapshot" or "## Career and motivation". Those are judgments their author writes
deliberately, not inferences an unattended agent makes at 18:45.

## Commitments
Only commitments go in checkboxes, only in daily notes, only in this form:
- [ ] text [owner:: me|them] [to:: Name] [from:: Name] [due:: YYYY-MM-DD]
`- [-]` means cancelled and is excluded from every metric. Never mirror a commitment
into a person file; the metrics count 01-Daily only and a mirror double counts it.

## Never record
Third party allegations attributed to a source. Flight risk or attrition predictions
tied to a name. Performance verdicts or termination or promotion speculation. Comp
figures. Health, family, immigration status, or any protected characteristic. Anything
touching an HR complaint, investigation or legal matter. Motive attribution.
Unreleased financials, reorgs or M&A.

## Output
End every run with a changelog: files created, files appended to, stubs created,
CONFLICTs flagged, questions for me. Nothing else.
